# GROUP_ID calendar

> A planned group's capacity draft: it produces no course progress and changes no course's lifecycle.
> On activation the budget must be re-decided from the previous group's closing evidence and the user's
> confirmation.

## The cycle container

State the cycle shape this group uses (for example `3-1-3`: block A input, a rest day, block B
integration), and whether a rest day repays debt. The container comes from the student profile and is not
reinvented in this file.

## Cycle schedule

| Cycle | COURSE_ID: block A → block B | Other member tracks |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | input content → integration content | that cycle's action |
| 2 | | |

A member whose capacity is undecided is written as "to be added at the activation review"; this table
promises it no frequency.

## Decidable thresholds

The closing review reads this section, and the conditions must be mechanically decidable:

1. Each member's minimum-count attainment rate.
2. The cap on total time-budget deviation.
3. The cap on days that failed to start.
4. The number of major-adjustment windows executed.

## External authority

This calendar schedules study and audit activities only. A fact belonging to an external system (trading,
work, health, and so on) is still governed by its own external source of truth; see
`main/50_playbook/cross_repo_reference.md`.
